  {
    "id": "comment-resolution",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "tab-interval-example",
    "name": "Resolution semantics: cycle clears on state-changing transitions only",
    "info": "An active cycle starts when a transition snapshot or interval signal is dispatched to dfsm-active.\nIt resolves only when a later accepted dfsm-activate request causes a real state change.\n\nSame-state retrigger requests do NOT resolve the cycle:\n  - They emit an active_transition snapshot with changed=false, retrigger=true.\n  - inFlightUnresolved stays true.\n  - Interval ticks continue to be skipped (skip) or coalesced (queue_one).\n\nInterval emissions are lifecycle signals, not transitions:\n  - They carry lifecycleType='active_interval'.\n  - They do not advance eventId.\n  - They do not mutate transition state (changed, retrigger, eventId).\n  - They are not same-state retriggers.",
    "x": 350,
    "y": 1200,
    "wires": []
  },
